## Core principle

We use local UI components from `@/components/ui` for all major UI elements and Tailwind CSS for all styling.

## Component usage

- **Must**: Use components from `@/components/ui` instead of native HTML elements where an equivalent exists. For example, use `<Button>` instead of `<button>`, and `<Typography>` for all text.
- **Must**: Use the `useToast()` hook from `@/components/ui` for all user notifications (success, error, info).
- **Icons**: Use icons from `react-icons/pi` to maintain visual consistency.

## Available components

The following components are available in `@/components/ui`:

- **Typography**: `Typography` with variants (heading, subtitle, body, label, number) and levels (1-4)
- **Button**: `Button` with variants (primary, secondary, tertiary) and sizes (sm, md, lg, icon)
- **Input**: `Input` with floating-label variant and label/startAdornment/endAdornment props
- **TextArea**: `TextArea` with floating-label variant
- **Select**: `Select` component for dropdowns
- **Dialog**: `AlertDialog`, `AlertDialogContent`, `AlertDialogHeader`, `AlertDialogDescription`, `AlertDialogFooter`
- **Drawer**: `Drawer`, `DrawerContent`, `DrawerHeader`, `DrawerTitle`, `DrawerDescription`, `DrawerFooter`, `DrawerClose`, `DrawerTrigger`
- **Tabs**: `TabList`, `TabItem` for tab navigation
- **Toast**: `Toaster`, `useToast` for notifications
- **Other**: `Skeleton`, `SkeletonTypography`, `Pill`, `CircularIcon`

## Styling with Tailwind CSS

- **Must**: All styling must be done with Tailwind CSS utility classes in the `className` prop.
- **Do not**: Write custom CSS files or use inline `style={{}}` objects.
- **Maintainability**: If you find yourself repeating the same combination of Tailwind classes on multiple elements, extract that element into a reusable React component ([Tailwind Best Practice](https://tailwindcss.com/docs/utility-first#maintainability-concerns)). Do not use `@apply`.
